The Linux Users' Group of Davis (LUGOD), will be holding our
9th anniversary meeting on:

  Monday
  January 21st, 2008
  6:30pm - 9:00pm


The meeting will be held at our regular location:

  Davis Public Library
  Blanchard Meeting Room
  315 East 14th Street
  Davis, California 95616


Presentation:

  "The Digital Tipping Point": it's all about you (LUGs)

  Presented by:
    Christian Einfeldt, Producer

  The "Digital Tipping Point" is a film project about the big changes
  that open source software will bring to our world.  Like the printing
  press before it, open source software will empower average people to
  create an immense wave of new literature, art, and science.

  This presentation will aquaint people with the "Digital Tipping Point."
  Christian will tell the odd story of how it got started, about the places
  that they have been, what they have accomplished so far, and what they
  need to finish the project.  He'll also discuss how one can use the DTP
  video for their own projects, or become part of the DTP crew.

  About the Speaker:
    Christian Einfeldt is a simple end user who proves daily that any
    knucklehead can use FOSS (free and open source software).
    He was motivated to move his law practice to FOSS in late 2000 out of a
    concern for viruses.  When he saw that FOSS represents a chance for
    humanity to practice sharing on a massive scale, he became convinced
    that he had to do his part to use video and the Internet to give the
    world some footage to fuel the conversation about what cyber freedom
    means and why it is important.  The Digital Tipping Point resulted.

  Also, join us in celebrating LUGOD's 9th year of serving the Davis
  community.  Free refreshments will be provided!


For details on this meeting, visit:

  http://www.lugod.org/meeting/


For maps, directions, public transportation schedules, etc., visit:

  http://www.lugod.org/meeting/library/


About LUGOD:

  The Linux Users' Group of Davis is a 501(c)7 non-profit organization
  dedicated to the Linux computer operating system and other Open Source
  and Free Software.

  LUGOD holds regular meetings with guest speakers in Davis, California,
  as well as other events in Davis and the greater Sacramento region.
  Events are always free and open to the public.

  Please visit our website for more details:  http://www.lugod.org/


-- 
Bill Kendrick
pr@lugod.org
Public Relations Officer
Linux Users' Group of Davis
http://www.lugod.org/

